# Integer16 literal below the minimum

Verifies a negated int16 literal whose unsigned part exceeds the 16-bit
range is rejected with a compile-time diagnostic through the complete CLI
pipeline, consistent with int8 and int64.

>>> source
too_small: int16 = -32768
print(too_small)

<<< stdout

<<< stderr
eck: invalid literal `32768` for type `int16`: number too large to fit in target type at Span { start: 20, end: 25 }

<<< exit
1
